        "content": "Run `python3 monitoring/autoscale/run.py run` for CPU scale-out; add `--trigger latency` for two consecutive settled p95 cohorts above 500 ms. This is a shared benchmark controller, **not native Kubernetes HPA**. Both modes keep CPU-based scale-in: 60 seconds below 70% average target. CPU target is 1.25\u00d7 warmup median (minimum 50m), capped at two units and one cycle. Java adds an order pod; Wasm adds a whole serving host. CPU scopes differ. Latency decisions include cohort/settling/export delay. The report separates trigger, direct new-pod order, serving capacity, traffic recovery and downscale. Forced final cleanup is not automatic scaling."
